From fd559354072e81f0493f21318e61b3a196ee4bc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:34:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion): bore-side Contour ramp entry holds the ramp
 angle

On a closed ring the Ramp arm's chord had no run, so each level fed
straight down at the cutting feed with no note. The chord now stands only
where it is no steeper than the links' ramp angle (3 deg by default);
otherwise the ramp zig-zags along the lead-in and ring at that angle, and
a path too short for it dives by name at the plunge feed.

Fixes #1664

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
